# The UI shell requires no environment variables. Activation sessions require
# the explicit server-only development settings in docs/activation/wire-review.md.
# Managed Portal configuration awaits verified runtime, schema and secret facilities.
# Do not invent tenant endpoints or copy credentials here.
# Never expose provider or database secrets through browser VITE_* variables.

# Optional SERVER-ONLY credential for the read-only inspector (private repositories).
# The inspector reads GITHUB_TOKEN from its process environment, not VITE_*.
# server/index.mjs does not load .env automatically. Export it before starting,
# or use Node's --env-file=/absolute/private/file option. Never commit its value.
# The credential must already have access to the intended repository and contents.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Optional local activation intake candidate. Requires ACTIVATION_DEV=1 and its
# existing scoped principal/token/admission bundle. Default remains disabled.
# ACTIVATION_INTAKE=1
# Hosted interpretation reuses server-only PORTAL_LLM_ENDPOINT, PORTAL_LLM_MODEL,
# PORTAL_LLM_API_KEY and PORTAL_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS (or OPENAI_API_KEY at default endpoint).
# No valid provider => labeled deterministic review-checklist fallback.
